{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2022-05-25 16:30:00', 'title': "INSTALLATION OF POWERLINE SAFETY SETTINGS ESSENTIALLY COMPLETE IN HIGH-FIRE RISK AREAS ACROSS 25,500 DISTRIBUTION LINE MILES IN PG&E'S SERVICE AREA", 'text': 'OAKLAND, CALIF.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT INSTALLATION OF ENHANCED POWERLINE SAFETY SETTINGS (EPSS) ON ITS DISTRIBUTION POWERLINES IN HIGH FIRE-RISK AREAS (HFRA) IS ESSENTIALLY COMPLETE. THESE SAFETY SETTINGS QUICKLY AND AUTOMATICALLY SHUT OFF POWER WITHIN ONE-TENTH OF A SECOND OR LESS IF A POTENTIAL THREAT IS DETECTED TO THE ELECTRIC SYSTEM, SUCH AS A TREE BRANCH FALLING INTO A POWERLINE. PG&E METEOROLOGY AND OPERATIONS TEAMS ASSESS'}